# Cyris schedule — supercronic fires at container-local clock (TZ set in compose).
#
# The tick is hourly and unconditional; `--if-due` asks the effective digest
# schedule (the `settings` table of the SQLite file on a local install, of D1 on d1) whether this hour is a digest hour, and derives --period from
# which of the two it is.
# A fixed `0 8,20` line could not do that: this file is baked into the image, so
# changing the times would mean a rebuild.
# `ingest` stores what the feeds hold every hour, so the store is the RSS buffer a
# feed's few-hour snapshot cannot be (ADR-0001). It shares the digest's line so the
# digest reads what this hour's poll just stored; two lines would run at once, and the
# digest could start before the poll has finished. `;` rather than `&&`: a failed poll must not skip the digest.
0 * * * * cyris ingest --config /app/cyris.toml --sources /app/sources.yaml; cyris run --if-due --config /app/cyris.toml --sources /app/sources.yaml
# promote-sync: hourly
0 * * * * cyris promote-sync --config /app/cyris.toml --sources /app/sources.yaml
